1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,280
READING TASK

2
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:06,400
The Story of an Eyewitness by Jack London

3
00:00:07,380 --> 00:00:10,900
Never before in history has a city been so completely destroyed.

4
00:00:11,860 --> 00:00:13,240
San Francisco is gone.

5
00:00:19,880 --> 00:00:21,240
Its businesses are gone.

6
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:25,860
The factories, hotels and palaces are all gone too.

7
00:00:35,720 --> 00:00:37,380
The sun was red in the dark sky.

8
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:39,600
There was no stopping the fires.

9
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:42,800
There was no way to organize or communicate.

10
00:00:44,080 --> 00:00:46,540
The steel railway tracks were now useless.

11
00:00:46,540 --> 00:00:51,100
And the great pipes for carrying water under the streets had burst.

12
00:01:00,180 --> 00:01:02,020
Out at sea it was calm.

13
00:01:02,580 --> 00:01:04,300
No wind came up.

14
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:06,540
Yet from every direction - east,

15
00:01:06,840 --> 00:01:11,620
west, north, and south, strong winds blew upon the unlucky city.

16
00:01:12,320 --> 00:01:16,000
Man himself had to make ruins of some of the city’s best buildings

17
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:19,180
so that they would not be a danger to those in the streets.

18
00:01:20,280 --> 00:01:24,680
A list of buildings undestroyed was now only a few addresses.

19
00:01:26,060 --> 00:01:28,880
A list of the brave men and women would fill a library.

20
00:01:30,040 --> 00:01:32,760
A list of all those killed will never be made.

21
00:01:34,520 --> 00:01:38,180
Amazing as it may seem, Wednesday night was a quiet night.

22
00:01:38,380 --> 00:01:39,520
There were no crowds.

23
00:01:40,360 --> 00:01:43,860
The policemen said nothing; even their horses were quiet.

24
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:47,860
There were no shouts or people doing crazy things.

25
00:01:48,560 --> 00:01:52,960
In all those terrible hours I saw not one woman who cried,

26
00:01:52,960 --> 00:01:55,300
not one man who was excited.

27
00:01:56,380 --> 00:01:58,600
Before the fires, through the night,

28
00:01:59,020 --> 00:02:02,360
thousands and thousands of people who had lost their homes left

29
00:02:02,360 --> 00:02:03,180
for safety.

30
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:05,460
Some were covered in blankets.

31
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:10,440
Sometimes whole families put everything they owned and could save into wagons.

32
00:02:11,440 --> 00:02:14,800
They helped one another climb the high hills around the city.

33
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:20,820
Never in all San Francisco’s history were her people so kind as on

34
00:02:20,820 --> 00:02:22,080
that terrible night.
